        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12457039/comment/12836880",
          "id": "12836880",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=digydigy",
            "name": "digydigy",
            "key": "digydigy",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Digy",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Besides passing docid+fieldname to FVH, can there be another method that accepts the original text to be highlighted?\nlike:\n{code}\n\tgetBestFragment( final FieldQuery fieldQuery, IndexReader reader, String originalText, int fragCharSize ) \n{code}\nSo, the field content can be stored outside of lucene resulting in  a smaller index.\n\nDIGY",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=digydigy",
            "name": "digydigy",
            "key": "digydigy",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Digy",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2010-02-22T20:15:28.008+0000",
          "updated": "2010-02-22T20:15:28.008+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12457039/comment/12836988",
          "id": "12836988",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=koji",
            "name": "koji",
            "key": "koji",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=koji&avatarId=36506",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=koji&avatarId=36506",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=koji&avatarId=36506",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=koji&avatarId=36506"
            },
            "displayName": "Koji Sekiguchi",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Tokyo"
          },
          "body": "getBestFragment() method needs docId and fieldName in order to get a TermPositionVector object from IndexReader when trying to make snippets.\n\nFVH could be acceptable an array of String so that it can make snippets from String[] outside of Lucene, rather than stored values. But it is out of this thread.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=koji",
            "name": "koji",
            "key": "koji",
            "avatarUrls": {
